    {
      "v": 8,
      "zh": "王从御园回到酒席之处，见哈曼伏在以斯帖所靠的榻上；王说：「他竟敢在宫内、在我面前凌辱王后吗？」这话一出王口，人就蒙了哈曼的脸。",
      "en": "When the king returned from the palace garden to the banquet of wine, Haman was throwing himself down[NOTE:1] on the couch where Esther was lying.[NOTE:2] The king exclaimed, “Will he also attempt to rape the queen while I am still in the building?”As these words left the king’s mouth, they covered Haman’s face.",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “falling”; NAB, NRSV “had (+ just TEV) thrown himself (+ down TEV).”",
        "Heb “where Esther was” (so KJV, NASB). The term “lying” has been supplied in the translation for stylistic reasons; cf. NAB, NIV, NRSV, NLT “was reclining.”"
